I agree with most of what's been said already. I personally though
would check out the first three levels before doing anything, to see
if there's an altar nearby. I'd dilute the PoSI to water, bless them
both and use them to bless the magic marker and PoGA. If you can find
more potions to convert into holy water (maybe from stores
discovered?) you could bless the SoEA, and if I did find other potions
before an altar (that I was willing to use up), I might not dilute the
PoSI and instead bless it.

As people have said re: what item to enchant, the robe will be with
you for a long while. You mentioned, though, that the scroll was
actually Enchant Weapon, and if I didn't find access to holy water
quickly I'd use it on the staff, since even that +1 would be a big
help in surviving those first three levels or so. I've gotta say,
though, if you can get that SoEW blessed, skip down to the mines just
long enough to relieve a gnome of his stack of 4 daggers, blessing
those all at once can be great fun. Give one of them a different name
from the others so they don't stack, so you can melee with one and
toss the rest at your hapless enemies.

As for the rings, I'd only use the FR when necessary... if you find
ample food, then I'd use the RoP, but when I've got an adventurer that
forgot to pack his lunch, I play things very conservatively. I don't
think the +1 will make enough of a difference to be worth it (again,
unless you score some eats).

Basically, I wouldn't use anything without scouting around a bit first
to see what the options are, but if you get into trouble, hey, use all
the tools in your arsenal!

